span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></span><!--]-->. (<!--[--><!--[-->2015<!--]--><!--]-->). <!--[--><!--[-->DOWNY MILDEW RESISTANT 6 and DMR6-LIKE OXYGENASE 1 are partially redundant but distinct suppressors of immunity in Arabidopsis<!--]--><!--]-->. <!--[--><i class="References__source">Plant J.</i><!--]--><!--[--><!--[-->81<!--]--><!--]-->, <!--[--><!--[-->210<!--]--><!--]-->–<!--[--><!--[-->222<!--]--><!--]-->. doi: <!--[--><!--[-->10.1111/tpj.12719<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><ul class="References__links"><!----><li class="References__links__item"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1111/tpj.12719" target="_blank" data-event="articleReference-a-crossRef">CrossRef </a></li><li class="References__links__item"><a href="http://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?author=T..%2BZeilmaker&amp;author=N.%2BR..%2BLudwig&amp;author=J..%2BElberse&amp;author=M.%2BF..%2BSeidl&amp;author=L..%2BBerke&amp;author=A..%2BVan%2BDoorn&amp;publication_year=2015&amp;title=DOWNY%2BMILDEW%2BRESISTANT%2B6%2Band%2BDMR6-LIKE%2BOXYGENASE%2B1%2Bare%2Bpartially%2Bredundant%2Bbut%2Bdistinct%2Bsuppressors%2Bof%2Bimmunity%2Bin%2BArabidopsis&amp;journal=Plant+J.&amp;volume=81&amp;pages=210-222" target="_blank" data-event="articleReference-a-googleScholar">Google Scholar</a></li><!----></ul></div></li><li class="References__item" id="B94"><div class="References__label"><p>94</p></div><div class="References__content"><p class="notranslate"><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span person-group-type="author" class="References__personGroup"><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__name"><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__surname">Zhang</span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__givenNames">Y.</span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__name"><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__surname">Li</span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__givenNames">D.</span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__name"><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__surname">Zhang</span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__givenNames">H.</span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__name"><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__surname">Hong</span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__givenNames">Y.</span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__name"><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__surname">Huang</span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__givenNames">L.</span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__name"><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__surname">Liu</span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="References__givenNames">S.</span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><span class="ReferencesList_etal">et al</span><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></span><!--]-->. (<!--[--><!--[-->2015<!--]--><!--]-->). <!--[--><!--[-->Tomato histone H2B monoubiquitination enzymes SlHUB1 and SlHUB2 contribute to disease resistance against Botrytis cinerea through modulating the balance between SA- and JA/ET-mediated signaling pathways<!--]--><!--]-->. <!--[--><i class="References__source">BMC Plant Biol.</i><!--]--><!--[--><!--[-->15<!--]--><!--]-->, <!--[--><!--[-->252<!--]--><!--]-->. doi: <!--[--><!--[-->10.1186/s12870-015-0614-2<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><ul class="References__links"><!----><li class="References__links__item"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1186/s12870-015-0614-2" target="_blank" data-event="articleReference-a-crossRef">CrossRef </a></li><li class="References__links__item"><a href="http://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?author=Y..%2BZhang&amp;author=D..%2BLi&amp;author=H..%2BZhang&amp;author=Y..%2BHong&amp;author=L..%2BHuang&amp;author=S..%2BLiu&amp;publication_year=2015&amp;title=Tomato%2Bhistone%2BH2B%2Bmonoubiquitination%2Benzymes%2BSlHUB1%2Band%2BSlHUB2%2Bcontribute%2Bto%2Bdisease%2Bresistance%2Bagainst%2BBotrytis%2Bcinerea%2Bthrough%2Bmodulating%2Bthe%2Bbalance%2Bbetween%2BSA-%2Band%2BJA%2FET-mediated%2Bsignaling%2Bpathways&amp;journal=BMC+Plant+Biol.&amp;volume=15" target="_blank" data-event="articleReference-a-googleScholar">Google Scholar</a></li><!----></ul></div></li><!--]--></ul></div><!--]--><!----><div class="Summary"><h2 class="acc-hidden">Summary</h2><!--[--><p class="h5">Keywords</p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[-->Xylella<!--]--><!--[-->, <!--]--><!--]--><!--[--><!--[-->olive<!--]--><!--[-->, <!--]--><!--]--><!--[--><!--[-->resistance<!--]--><!--[-->, <!--]--><!--]--><!--[--><!--[-->SSR<!--]--><!--[-->, <!--]--><!--]--><!--[--><!--[-->genotyping<!--]--><!--[-->, <!--]--><!--]--><!--[--><!--[-->parentage analysis<!--]--><!--[-->, <!--]--><!--]--><!--[--><!--[-->transcriptomic<!--]--><!----><!--]--><!--]--></p><!--]--><!--[--><p class="h5">Citation</p><p>La Notte P, Saponari M, Mousavi S, Mariotti R, Abou Kubaa R, Nikbakht R, Melcarne G, Specchia F, Altamura G, Ligorio A, Boscia D, Surano A, Saldarelli P and Giampetruzzi A (2024) <!--[-->A survey in natural olive resources exposed to high inoculum pressure indicates the presence of traits of resistance to <i>Xylella fastidiosa</i> in Leccino offspring<!--]-->. <i>Front. Plant Sci.</i> 15:1457831. doi: <a class="Summary__doi notranslate" target="_blank" href="http://dx.doi.org/10.3389/fpls.2024.1457831" data-event="articleSummary-a-doi">10.3389/fpls.2024.1457831</a></p><!--]--><!----><!--[--><div class="Summary__dates"><div><p class="h5">Received</p><p>01 July 2024</p></div><!----><div><p class="h5">Accepted</p><p>29 August 2024</p></div><div><p class="h5">Published</p><p>30 September 2024</p></div><!----><!----><!----><div><p class="h5">Volume</p><p>15 - 2024</p></div></div><!----><div><p class="h5">Edited by</p><!--[--><p class="notranslate"> Giovanni Ca